{{define "apps.gohtml"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>School ERP — staff apps</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/app.css?v={{.AssetVersion}}">
{{template "themeboot"}}
</head>
<body class="marketing apps">

<header class="topbar">
  <span class="wordmark">School ERP</span>
  <span class="spacer"></span>
  {{template "themebtn"}}
  <a class="quiet" href="/login">Sign in</a>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="apps-hero">
    <h1>Staff apps for Android</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Two apps run on school handsets rather than in a browser. They are not on
      Google Play yet, so they are installed from here. Open this page
      <strong>on the phone the app will live on</strong> and tap Download.
    </p>
  </section>

  {{if not .AnyAvailable}}
  <p class="apps-none" role="status">
    {{if .AnyStatic}}
    No build has been published to this server yet. The downloads below are the
    builds that ship with the site itself.
    {{else}}
    No build has been published to this server yet. Nothing to install today —
    check back, or ask the school's supplier.
    {{end}}
  </p>
  {{end}}

  <section class="apps-list" aria-label="Available apps">
    {{range .Apps}}
    <article class="app-card{{if and (not .Available) (not .Static)}} unbuilt{{end}}">
      <div class="app-head">
        <h2>{{.Name}}</h2>
        {{if .Available}}<span class="app-version">v{{.Version}}</span>{{end}}
      </div>
      <p class="app-tagline">{{.Tagline}}</p>

      <p class="app-who"><span class="app-label">Goes on</span> {{.Who}}</p>
      <ul class="app-needs">
        {{range .Needs}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}
      </ul>

      {{if .Available}}
      <a class="app-dl" href="/apps/{{.Slug}}.apk" rel="nofollow">
        Download {{.Size}}
      </a>
      <dl class="app-facts">
        <dt>Built</dt><dd>{{.Built}}</dd>
        <dt>File</dt><dd>{{.File}}</dd>
        {{if .SHA256}}<dt>SHA-256</dt><dd class="app-sum">{{.SHA256}}</dd>{{end}}
      </dl>
      {{else if .Static}}
      <a class="app-dl" href="{{.Static}}" rel="nofollow">Download</a>
      <p class="app-pending">
        This build is served as a static file with the site. No version, size,
        build date or checksum is published for it.
      </p>
      {{else}}
      <p class="app-pending">Not published to this server yet.</p>
      {{end}}
    </article>
    {{end}}
  </section>

  <section class="apps-howto">
    <h2>Installing it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap <strong>Download</strong> above on the phone itself.</li>
      <li>Open the downloaded file. Android will say it cannot install apps from
          this source — that is expected, and it says it for everything that did
          not come from Play.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Settings</strong> on that message and turn on
          <strong>Allow from this source</strong> for your browser. Turn it back
          off afterwards if you like; the app keeps working.</li>
      <li>Go back and tap <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
      <li>Open the app and register it — the steps are just below.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="register">Registering the phone</h2>
    <p>
      Neither app does anything at all until the school lets it in. Since
      August 2026 that happens on the handset itself, with the phone number and
      PIN the office issued you — there is no code to type in ten minutes and
      nobody to telephone.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the app and enter your <strong>mobile number</strong> and
          <strong>PIN</strong>. If you do not have a PIN, the school office
          issues one from your staff record.</li>
      <li><strong>Bus Tracker only:</strong> type the <strong>number painted on
          the bus</strong> you are driving — TS07UA1234, spaces or no spaces,
          upper or lower case. That is what tells the school which vehicle this
          phone is on, so nobody has to pick a bus off a list at six in the
          morning.</li>
      <li>The phone now appears at the school as <strong>waiting for
          approval</strong>, and reports nothing until it is let in.</li>
      <li><strong>The principal</strong> approves it — transport screen for a
          bus, SMS gateway screen for the office phone. For the gateway, an
          administrator who registers it themselves is approved as they go.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="apps-note">
      A bus tracker is a live map of where children are during the day, so
      there is no approve-yourself shortcut on it: only the principal or a
      platform administrator can let one start reporting, whoever registered
      it. That is also why this page needs no password. The file on its own is
      inert — it reaches nothing until a named person at the school says yes.
    </p>

    <h2>Checking what you downloaded</h2>
    <p>
      Sideloaded apps get no store check on the way in, so the SHA-256 above is
      the only proof the file is ours. Anyone who wants to verify it can, on a
      computer:
    </p>
    <pre class="apps-code">sha256sum bus-tracker-1.0.0.apk</pre>
    <p>
      If it does not match the figure on this page character for character, do
      not install it.
    </p>

    <h2>When these reach Google Play</h2>
    <p>
      This page stays. A school that has already installed from here keeps
      working, and Play becomes the easier of two routes rather than a migration
      anyone has to perform.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

{{template "themejs"}}
</body>
</html>{{end}}
